           TestAbsCents_SignIndependent
The >= 3 threshold and the sign-independence are both genuinely guarded.

FINDING F1 (AC1, spec-wording deviation, behaviour more permissive than
SPEC §2.2): §2.2 says "count shared KEYS per account"; Detect counts matching
ROWS (importer.go:110-118 increments `shared[id]` once per candidate ROW that
hits the account's key SET). A single distinct coincidentally-shared key
repeated 3x in the import file therefore reaches the threshold. Probe
(scratch, since removed):
  ledger  = {2026-01-01 Amazon -9.99 [checking], 2026-01-20 Utterly Unrelated -123.45 [checking]}
  candidate = the Amazon row 3x + 2 unrelated rows
  Detect(...) -> {AccountID:checking AccountName:USAA Checking Reason:}
Under the spec's literal reading that should be "no match" (one shared key).
No AC1 case enumerates this, and the real-data check detects correctly, so I
do not read it as a FAIL — it is a lead ruling on wording vs implementation.

