FINDING F3 (AC3, TOCTOU — probed at the lead's request, NOT a regression).
The identical-content scan runs outside the exclusive write. Two CONCURRENT
uploads of byte-identical content under DIFFERENT names both scan before
either writes, so both land:
  probe result: "both identical-content files landed in 20/20 concurrent rounds"
Master has no identical check at all, so master writes both too — IM2 is no
worse concurrently and strictly better sequentially, and §2.2 claims no
atomicity. Backlog item, not a defect against AC3.

