MODIFIED PRE-EXISTING TEST #1 — TestHandleImport_MixedBatchDeletesOnlyImported.
Scrutinised as instructed. The diff is confined to ONE line plus a comment:
`good := seedImportFile(t, importDir, "good.csv", importCSV)` became a distinct
`goodCSV` constant. No assertion changed: the 4-outcome length check, the
status map {good.csv:imported, dupe.csv:skipped, notes.txt:rejected,
../escape.csv:rejected} and all four source/destination existence checks are
byte-identical. I proved the change is FORCED by intended behaviour, not
masking a bug: reverting the fixture to `importCSV` in the scratch copy yields
  handlers_test.go:3076: good.csv: Status="skipped" want "imported" (reason "identical to dupe.csv")
i.e. exactly §2.2's cross-name identical-skip, the same behaviour
TestHandleImport_UnassignedIdenticalContentSkipsAcrossNames pins deliberately.

MODIFIED PRE-EXISTING TEST #2 — TestImportOneFile_ProductionWriteBindingIsExclusive.
Only the skipped-reason whitelist was widened. The invariant is intact and still
asserted verbatim: `imported != 1` -> t.Fatalf, `skipped != goroutines-1` ->
t.Fatalf, `other != 0` -> t.Fatalf, source survives, destination content equals
the untouched source, over 10 rounds x 16 goroutines.
  - baseline: `go test -race -count=20 -run TestImportOneFile_ProductionWriteBindingIsExclusive ./internal/handlers/explorer/`
    -> `ok  budget2/internal/handlers/explorer  1.846s` (no race reports)
  - the widening is NECESSARY, not cosmetic: narrowing it back to master's single
    reason and running `-count=20` gives
      `import_binding_race_test.go:90: round 9: skipped outcome had unexpected reason "identical to race.csv"` (x5)
      --- FAIL
  - the widening did NOT weaken the guard: MUT-8 rebinding
    `defaultImportDeps().write` from `store.CreateExclusive` to `store.WriteFile`
    still gives
      `round 0: 16 of 16 goroutines reported imported (want exactly 1) — defaultImportDeps().write is no longer exclusive`
      --- FAIL
RULING ON THE STRAGGLER: "identical to race.csv" is correct behaviour here, not a
hidden race. All 16 goroutines import the SAME name with the SAME bytes, so a
straggler that observes the winner's file during its own content scan is telling
the truth (the destination already holds exactly what it would write) and still
writes nothing. The genuine TOCTOU that the arrangement exposes is F3 above
(different names, identical bytes, concurrent) — present on master too.

