========================= AC7 — Unassigned surfaces =========================
PASS, on both surfaces.
  - TestHandleImport_DetectedImportResultsInZeroUnassigned drives a real scan
    (Detected=="acctX"), posts the import, then asserts
    `loader.UnassignedCount() == 0` after a fresh `loader.LoadData()`.
  - SURFACE ENUMERATION (split-classification check, not diff-trust). Two
    independent "unassigned" renderers exist:
      (a) transaction count: dataloader.UnassignedCount -> dashboard/handlers.go:197
          and explorer/handlers.go:265 -> components/unassigned_banner.html
      (b) FILE list: handlers/accounts/handlers.go:599-603, `unassigned` =
          every basename with `matchByID[name] == ""`, where
          `matchByID[name] = accounts.MatchFile(accts, name)` (line 579)
    Both are downstream of ONE classifier, `accounts.MatchFile`, and IM2 refuses
    to write any detected file unless `accounts.MatchFile(accts, finalName) ==
    acct.ID` (MUT-4 proves that guard is live). Surface (b) therefore cannot list
    an IM2-written file. No third classifier exists.
  - LEAD'S REAL-DATA CHECK re-run by me against my scratch copy (cited as
    corroboration, not as my primary evidence):
      `python3 .swarm/tier3/IM2-fixture/check.py <scratch>/im2 preupload` -> exit 0, "== ALL PASS",
      including `PASS accounts page: no unassigned files`, the four generated
      names `usaa-credit-card_2026-07-01_to_2026-08-27.csv`,
      `usaa-credit-card_2026-07-01_to_2026-09-18.csv`,
      `usaa-checking_2026-07-06_to_2026-09-14.csv`,
      `usaa-credit-card_2024-08-02_to_2025-11-18.csv`,
      `PASS list_data_files count 17`, `PASS no browser-named file in data dir`.
      `... check.py <scratch>/im2 full` -> exit 0, "== ALL PASS".

FINDING F5 (lead artifact, NOT a worker defect). SPEC.md §4.2 says that against
the FULL fixture "all seven files must be flagged identical". The full run shows
SIX flagged identical; `bk_download (3).csv` is correctly NOT identical (it has
no byte-twin in the full fixture — its would-be twin
`usaa-credit-card_2026-07-01_to_2026-08-27.csv` is created only by the preupload
import). check.py itself encodes six, which is why it passes. SPEC §4.2 text
overstates; the worker's behaviour is right.

